# User guide (`/guide`)

Files: [`webapp/guide/ru.html`](webapp/guide/ru.html), [`webapp/guide/en.html`](webapp/guide/en.html)  
Served at `PUBLIC_BASE_URL/guide?lang=ru|en` (prod: https://bot.themarfa.name/guide).  
Entry from bot: **❓ Помощь** / `/feedback` → inline **Справка** / **Guide**.

## When to update

If **user-facing capabilities** change — anything a regular user sees or can do (not admin-only):

- new / removed / renamed menu buttons or commands;
- wizard steps, alert types, destinations, Premium gates or free limits;
- import / sync / schedule / watch / chat / history / cart behavior that users rely on;
- Help / feedback copy that points at the guide.

## What to do

1. Update **both** `webapp/guide/ru.html` and `webapp/guide/en.html` (TOC + matching sections). Keep beginner-friendly wording.
2. If menu paths changed — also [`docs/user-flow-map.ru.md`](docs/user-flow-map.ru.md) and README ([`user-flow-map.mdc`](user-flow-map.mdc), [`readme.mdc`](readme.mdc)).
3. Include guide HTML in the **same commit** as the feature change (when the user asks to commit).

## Skip

Internal refactors, admin/backoffice-only screens, analytics, deploy, bugfixes with no UX/copy change.

Authority: code + `locales/` — runtime; guide — onboarding for end users (derived, must not drift).
